# Where main's release to Google Play's internal testing track signs in
# (#308): Workload Identity Federation, so no key is kept anywhere. Both
# are public names, not credentials: Google gives the service account's
# token only to a GitHub OIDC token of bats-lang/quire for a push to main
# (the provider's attribute condition), so they are committed, as
# scripts/sync-clients.env commits the OAuth clients (#200).
# The Google Cloud project "Quire" (number 162611675413, ID
# spring-duality-395520); the service account has no Cloud IAM role,
# only Play's "Release apps to testing tracks" for Quire.
# Plain NAME=value lines: no quotes, no spaces.
PLAY_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROVIDER=projects/162611675413/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/github/providers/quire
PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=quire-play-release@spring-duality-395520.iam.gserviceaccount.com
PLAY_PACKAGE=dev.middlefield.quire
